WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.900
Multi-GPU success depends on the software stack understanding the available devices.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:15.104
Drivers, compute runtimes, inference engines, model formats, operating system, and libraries must agree on supported hardware and features.

00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:19.116
CUDA is a common NVIDIA compute platform.

00:00:19.116 --> 00:00:23.600
ROCm supports selected AMD hardware and operating-system combinations.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.084
Vulkan can provide cross-platform acceleration in compatible runtimes.

00:00:28.084 --> 00:00:32.568
Capability and maturity vary by device and workload.

00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:42.715
Apple Metal supports acceleration on Apple platforms, usually through integrated unified-memory designs rather than a conventional collection of discrete cards.

00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:49.559
Multi-device expectations from desktop GPU systems should not be assumed to transfer directly.

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:50.739
llama.

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:58.055
cpp provides multi-GPU concepts such as device selection and model splitting for supported backends.

00:00:58.055 --> 00:01:08.675
Server-oriented runtimes such as vLLM may offer parallel execution and scheduling at a high level, with different hardware and configuration requirements.

00:01:08.675 --> 00:01:16.935
Configuration includes visible devices, memory limits, split strategy, cache, precision, batch behavior, networking, and service controls.

00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:23.779
A copied command may be wrong for a different topology or runtime version.

00:01:23.779 --> 00:01:30.623
Maintain a known working combination of drivers, runtime, model, configuration, and operating system.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:37.467
Test upgrades, record versions, preserve rollback, and avoid changing several layers at once.

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:42.422
Software stability can determine whether expensive hardware is useful.

00:01:42.422 --> 00:01:49.738
Containers can improve repeatability but do not erase host-driver, device, kernel, and runtime requirements.

00:01:49.738 --> 00:01:57.054
Record both host and container environments, device visibility, mounted models, permissions, and launch configuration.
